The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
@Test
public void testNonSecureFunctionality() {
    // Non-secure test code
}

@Test
public void testSecureFunctionality() {
    // Secure test code
}
```
Reason:
The tests for secure and non-secure functionalities were not properly isolated, leading to conflicts during execution. The secure tests require specific configurations that were not being separated from the non-secure tests, causing authentication issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
@Category(SecurityTests.class)
@Test
public void testSecureFunctionality() {
    // Secure test code
}

@Category(NonSecurityTests.class)
@Test
public void testNonSecureFunctionality() {
    // Non-secure test code
}
```
Reason:
By categorizing the tests into separate modules for security and non-security, the patch ensures that secure tests are executed in isolation from non-secure tests, preventing any conflicts and authentication issues during testing.

